            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0000\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\n        \"F001:F003\",\n        \"F005\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Claim C0000 correctly covers the manufacturer's obligations under paragraph (c)(1). The proposed edit injects the separate evidentiary rule, extension authority, and notice timing provisions of paragraph (c)(2) into the summary of C0000. Paragraph (c)(2) is already independently represented by existing claims C0001, C0002, and C0003. Merging them into C0000 bloats the summary beyond the text of paragraph (1) and fixes no defect.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0001\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\n        \"F003\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Passage F003 specifically restricts refunding the purchase price to vehicles ('(B) for a vehicle, refund the purchase price...'). The proposal alters the remedy to apply to 'either a vehicle or replacement equipment', directly contradicting the statutory text. In addition, it improperly absorbs paragraph (c)(2) into the summary.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
